Hephaestus so I find these type of men kinda boring now, they need something else to make me interested, having a fire beard would be a good start. Plus I'm really not into his facial hair choice, though he's actually have one, which is pretty much better than the Oadenol's Codex cover.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what are shaving's ashes and maple seed's blade. The second paragraph is pretty evocative, I actually never thought about how Artifact crafting would look like to be honest, this will be pretty good study material for me.<br /> <br /> Ooooh, Jalith aka Fair Folk are more relatable and predictable than spirits. I really like her after reading Castebook: Dawn, especially funny since Demetheus in the same book thought the opposite of her regarding FF and spirits. And her wishing her blade would be more fit for throwing here is kinda hilarious, I really wonder if she's Supernal Thrown. I actually thought that she was a mortal at first when reading the Compass East comic, since Devil-Tiger and Autochthonian-aspected DB are all the rage back then so a woman with boomerangs and a jaguar doesn't strike me as Exalted material.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, the skycutter's name is Yokuka make me realize that I don't know what is the naming scheme of Artifact in Exalted. Is it mostly non-nonsensical fantasy names or literal translated one like Flying Silver Dream?<br /> <br /> As for the art, it's nice but nothing spectacular. I'll give this part THREE JEN!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/xPJN4S4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-10-2018, 04: