e":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T19:24:33-07:00","id":1205055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1204863#post1204863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could totally come up with Evocation names that are all just lines from Simon &amp; Garfunkel too!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sage of Time Understanding. Turbulent Water Bypass. Long Lost Bodyguard Prana. Naked Light Revelation Technique. 50 Means of Egress.<br /> <br /> I could do this all day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T21:15:36-07:00","id":1205085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1204787#post1204787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh yes, if I ever get an opportunity to use that I'm definitely being ohh so subtle about calling it The Sword of Silence</div> </div> </div> </div>My game uses it. Our characters make a point to talk about how our Professor Opal is full of hot air about her swordsmanship because we never saw her draw her blade.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T23:39:38-07:00","id":1205477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205085#post1205085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My game uses it. Our characters make a point to talk about how our Professor Opal is full of hot air about her swordsmanship because we never saw her draw her blade.</div> </div> </div> </div>What blade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:12:43-07:00","id":1205492,"title":"","content":"So the pre-Primodial War has The Dawn Time as a new name now. I thought colossi is one of those fantasy version of a real word like wild=wild, but it's actually the plural form of colossus......My English vocabulary still need much much work.<br /> <br /> The paragraph also mentions elementals, so they are not created from the shattered essence of those five big elementals in this Edition I assume?<br /> <br /> There also a bunch of non-human races and their weird artifacts, now I feel as thought Ex3 really likes to.....eh....invent news things on the spots? As in there are a bunch of names and short descriptions in pretty much each paragraph. Which is very much different from Ex2 who, for some weird reasons, keeps inventing news fluffs about old stuff, for example: &quot;Remember the Forgotten Blade that we mention on MoW's write-up, want to hear very detailed fluff on who craft it, when they craft it and why?&quot;. I think that I prefer Ex3 approach, since Ex2 just sucks the fun out of me with these long-ass chapter about the FA and Primordial War.<br /> <br /> Oh oh oh, the Chosen learns to use MM without any mention of Autochthon? Can it be true, that Exalted won't have to kiss that trash bin\u2019s butthole anymore?????<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna be optimistic though, the chance of Autotincan being the inventor of Exaltation and being cramp into anything crafting related by the writers are still too high until I see the Alchemical book. For now, I\u2019ll enjoy the fact that the Artifacts created in the war are the invention of the Exalted themselves instead handout from the tin can the Moutain Folk (urgh, why does anything Autochthon related always involve stealing heat from the Exalted and the Incarnae).<br /> <br /> Sorry about that, this is making some very unpleasant opinions of mine surfaced, I may just have to give this chapter a Nega-Je\u2026\u2026.Wait, did the next paragraph just says COLOSSAL WEAPONS, not magical weapons, not legendary weapons, but COLOSSAL!!?? Scrap that, I\u2019ll give this chapter a five Jen, even if everything else in the book are just fetallio on how great Autochthon is.<br /> <br /> Hmmmm, this Eternal Nova guy, being mentioned in the book as inventing a MA style and the first to discover Evocation, not to mention awakening Evocation with a touch all seems\u2026..a bit much I think.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m ridiculously impressed how this book can write about the First Age and there are not even a single mention of Autochthon, all these examples of the Exalted hosts crafting and exploring and meeting new challenges are so exciting. If this is written in Ex2, I\u2019ll probably need a puke bucket since the book will go out of its way to avoid mention anything about the Exalted and instead will wax endlessly about Neverborn, Yozi and Primordial. I think I understand why Infernal have such a hate-boner toward Ex3 now.<br /> <br /> This sentence is devoted to the person who namedrop the orichaclum throne that transform into a giant murder robot. May the Sanxing blessed you with endless happiness and when troubles comes knocking on your door, a thousand arms Guanyin will descend from heaven and social-fu the trouble into oblivion.<br /> <br /> The Age of Sorrow part is kinda predictable to be honest, civilization crumbling, can\u2019t reach the height of the First Age,\u2026etc.<br /> <br /> Eeeh, the Scarred Land section is really overwhelming me with all these examples, like, all the previous section has nothing but examples with a few fluff sentences in between, now it\u2019s even MORE examples. I just gonna skim them all, oh wait, it\u2019s the trash bin\u2019s eye in the last example, and the book still refuse to say what this thing actually can do except \u201cIt\u2019s suuuuper powerful man\u201d, this is already annoying enough, the fact that it\u2019s a typical RPG cursed object is even more infuriating, if I do find it I\u2019ll reforge it in a squat toilet.<br /> <br /> And now I reach the Magical Materials section, and WOW! That Mesoamerican art amazing. Gosh, it will be so good if each material having its own traditional artwork.<br /> <br /> Orichalcum: I wonder why it\u2019s called like that instead Sungold like the other materials. Moon-silver, Star-metal, Soul-steel and then\u2026.. Orichalcum is a little strange, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> The first fours themes are pretty obviously Sun-themes so my eyes kinda skipped over them, but the contrast (or harmony) between light and shadow is very interesting, I hope one of the Artifact in this book explore this side of Orichalcum.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what channel Essence/Sorcerous energies better actually mean, like, if you feed the Artifact one mote, it will use that mote more\u2026.efficiently? I just not sure if this will ever come up when homebrewing Evocations.<br /> <br /> Ooohh, the whole bringing down disasters is new for this edition I think? So many ideas are bubbling in my head when I read that line.<br /> That last paragraph kinda comes out of nowhere for me, greenish tint, baleful sorcerous essence? Who is channeling those essence, why was its tint is green? I\u2019m not really sure what this text is trying to tell me exactly.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver: Those sfx are really hard to imagine, ripple like troubled water? Oh dear, it still have an affinity for the Wyld, I hate Lunar as shoggoth or silver Fair Folk so I don\u2019t like this bit at all.<br /> Okaaay, I write so much for Orichalcum so this will look super bad. But that\u2019s it for Moonsilver, since I have no ideas what its theme are. I saw the words in the book, but my mind is a shamble trying to connect the dots, one moment it\u2019s secrecy then another it\u2019s fury and furry. I sense a dark time ahead for Lunar.<br /> <br /> Starmetal: The idea that starmetal are formed by Creation\u2019s anima is so very evocative, way better than soulsteel-for-Sidereal in previous edition. Aside from that, it\u2019s very much what I expect from starmetal so there are not much to talk about. I do wonder something though, if it\u2019s possible for Orichaclum to have Evocation that influence gods too? Since Zenith\u2019s anima and Charms has those as one of its themes.<br /> <br /> Soulsteel: I always thought the book use \u201cEnemies of the gods\u201d since the Exalted hosts and the gods fought a bunch of different enemies now instead of Primordial-all-the-time, but now I think it\u2019s more like a synonym for Primordial, probably?<br /> <br /> Well, suffering, disease, death, silence, darkness,\u2026etc. Pretty much in-theme for Soulsteel. Though looking at those keywords, I just find it\u2019s too funny that there are the idea of \u201cWhite Soulsteel\u201d, oh my weapon don\u2019t have tortured souls instead, but it can shoot maggots that burrow into your skull and lay eggs in it.<br /> <br /> Jade: is jade, red jade is hot, green jade is plant-ly, there\u2019s not much to talk about to be honest. Though some of the non-elemental keywords are very interesting, especially white jade, I mean, what does sleep and history have to do with earth exactly?<br /> <br /> Oh there is a sidebar, unlocking your boyfriend super powers by going out with him, sounds straight forward enough. That arrogant FA breastplate sounds amazing though, my Zenith gonna guilt-trip it into oblivion with the power of Black Claw. And there is an aquatic giant vessel called Brass Leviathan and an aquatic giant Lunar called Leviathan, both live in the West???? They should wrestling shirtless to see who deserved the title. Orca moon man vs mecha brass man, oh my gay.<br /> <br /> If you want extra themes for your Artifact, throw in some exotic material. Hmmm, a staff whose theme is age/longevity and it has a peach on the tip, could it be\u2026?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/nQyPiTF.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Conclusion: This chapter is such a roller-coaster for me, there is pure rage and there is ultimate joy. But anything that mention COLOSSAL WEAPONS deserves a five Jen!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bHZIxaW.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T03:38:07-07:00","id":1205523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205492#post1205492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The paragraph also mentions elementals, so they are not created from the shattered essence of those five big elementals in this Edition I assume?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Core even goes so far as to suggest that the Elementals may be <i>older than</i> the gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205492#post1205492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that I prefer Ex3 approach, since Ex2 just sucks the fun out of me with these long-ass chapter about the FA and Primordial War.</div> </div> </div> </div>No kidding; the number of city writeups in Creation that <i>need</i> a discussion of what it was like prior to the Primordial War should be able to be counted on one hand.<br /> <br /> (Rathess. The answer is, it's just Rathess.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205492#post1205492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm, this Eternal Nova guy, being mentioned in the book as\u2026 awakening Evocation with a touch all seems\u2026..a bit much I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check in the Core, &quot;Wake the Sleeper.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T04:24:15-07:00","id":1205529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205492#post1205492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Orichalcum: I wonder why it\u2019s called like that instead Sungold like the other materials. Moon-silver, Star-metal, Soul-steel and then\u2026.. Orichalcum is a little strange, isn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt probably <i>would</i> fit the pattern of the others, but orichalcum has some literary background; it's the name of the yellow-coloured metal that Plato said was the basis of the wealth and power of Atlantis, so it tends to be referenced in a number of fantasy works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T04:27:20-07:00","id":1205530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205492#post1205492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooohh, the whole bringing down disasters is new for this edition I think? So many ideas are bubbling in my head when I read that line.<br /> That last paragraph kinda comes out of nowhere for me, greenish tint, baleful sorcerous essence? Who is channeling those essence, why was its tint is green? I\u2019m not really sure what this text is trying to tell me exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prolonged contact with demonic energies tends to give orichalcum that tint. Demons are big on that, as are some solars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-11-2018, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:06:52-07:00","id":1206381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205529#post1205529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt probably <i>would</i> fit the pattern of the others, but orichalcum has some literary background; it's the name of the yellow-coloured metal that Plato said was the basis of the wealth and power of Atlantis, so it tends to be referenced in a number of fantasy works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's actually real thing, pretty interesting actually. I just google all the other MM and turns out adamant is also a real mythical metal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205530#post1205530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prolonged contact with demonic energies tends to give orichalcum that tint. Demons are big on that, as are some solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if that's just cosmetic, I can't think of any Evocations ideas from reading that sentence aside from enhancing demon summoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:21:06-07:00","id":1206385,"title":"","content":"(It's a nod to infernals)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:30:40-07:00","id":1206389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1206385#post1206385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It's a nod to infernals)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which has the nice extra background that orichalcum has also been used to describe brass, a demon city's favorite, not only the gold-ish copper of its greek and roman etimology.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:34:06-07:00","id":1206392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1205085#post1205085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My game uses it. Our characters make a point to talk about how our Professor Opal is full of hot air about her swordsmanship because we never saw her draw her blade.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Steven Universe fan, I am amused that someone named Opal uses the Forgotten Blade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:35:01-07:00","id":1206393,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I wonder how my demon-hating orichaclum-loving Zenith should react to this new infomation.<br /> <br /> Speaking of adamant, there are no mentions of it in the MM section at all. I wonder if they decided that it's just merely an exotic material now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:38:44-07:00","id":1206395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1206393#post1206393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I wonder how my demon-hating orichaclum-loving Zenith should react to this new infomation.<br /> <br /> Speaking of adamant, there are no mentions of it in the MM section at all. I wonder if they decided that it's just merely an exotic material now?</div> </div> </div> </div>An obsession with purity? Well, Orichalcum doesn't just go green. It requires prolonged exposure and all. It's almost a marker for excess radiation, except it's demons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:43:10-07:00","id":1206397,"title":"","content":"I'm personally less inclined to see Infernals in the reference, but mostly because I'm burned out on discussion of Infernals getting into every damn thing. My God, I remember when somebody went on about the Lunar Tell being something they inherited from damn Oramus*!<br /> <br /> \u200bTo my eyes, the significance of the whole &quot;pre-humans channelled fell sorceries through it&quot; thing is to place the wishmetal into a context before it was wielded by Solars, and the image of it developing a Verdigris as a result is just a quirky interaction between a magical material and weird energies. Also because green is one of the cooler looking oxidations, which is why nobody complains that the Statue of Liberty isn't brown and lustrous anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1206393#post1206393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I wonder how my demon-hating orichaclum-loving Zenith should react to this new infomation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they could see it as something that Solars reclaimed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of adamant, there are no mentions of it in the MM section at all. I wonder if they decided that it's just merely an exotic material now?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAs I recall, it's still considered a magical material, just that with no Exalted tied to it that wasn't the best place to introduce it.<br /> <br /> * That someone was me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:45:19-07:00","id":1206473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1206397#post1206397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAs I recall, it's still considered a magical material, just that with no Exalted tied to it that wasn't the best place to introduce it.</div> </div> </div> </div>More precisely, with no previously-mentioned-in-3E Exalted tied to it, it wasn't the best place to introduce it. (Adamant Caste Alchemicals are tied to it, but Arms isn't the place to introduce Alchemicals.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T09:03:13-07:00","id":1206482,"title":"","content":"Is it normal for the MM to be associated with the Exalted on such a level that Adamant is excluded from the book just because there is no Exalted tied to it?<br /> <br /> Though reading about Adamant theme, I can see that most of the keywords has quite an overlap with Moonsilver and Blue Jade so there is no much loss if Adamant do not appear. Those wordcount can be used for much more useful thing, like All-Conquering Colossus for example :'3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1206397#post1206397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they could see it as something that Solars reclaimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, this will fit him perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T10:16:31-07:00","id":1206505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1203459#post1203459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depend on what kind of boys does he like, I can only deal with so much bishonen in my entertainment...</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know that if we ever found ourselves in Creation Jen, we could wingman each other, since we\u2019d never be in competition for the same guys...<br /> <br /> *Ledaal Kes fanclub president*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T13:07:48-07:00","id":1206996,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that The Five Magical Materials were named such by the Exalted Host during the First Age because they could more easily draw forth power from them and their relative abundancy, not because those particular materials are &quot;mystically elevated above all other magic substances&quot; or anything. That said, going by that logic, I have no idea why Soulsteel makes the cut to belong either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T14:23:49-07:00","id":1207015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1203042#post1203042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the perspective of the image and the meaning of the player finding a treasure trove of Artifact in this book like this lady founds her in the building.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if I told you I could speak to her to see if she can set you up with some of the shiny personalities* inside. As the Chosen of Silence, she knows her way around the corners of the Creation that have fallen silent since good old days, as much as she does around the awkward silences between your sparkling thoughts and embarrassing utterances. Sounds like a good person to go to for first date advice, no?<br /> <br /> *Maybe even with Gorgon or Unison! Well essentially anyone, but the Stormcaller cause you see, that guy is kinda loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/81-vx3","name":"VX3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar81_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:27:37-07:00","id":1207051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1206996#post1206996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that The Five Magical Materials were named such by the Exalted Host during the First Age because they could more easily draw forth power from them and their relative abundancy, not because those particular materials are &quot;mystically elevated above all other magic substances&quot; or anything. That said, going by that logic, <b>I have no idea why Soulsteel makes the cut to belong either.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>had</i> the idea, though, right there in your previous sentence. You can draw forth power from soulsteel. Only two of the Exalt types we know about from the time were Dissonant with it, and even a Dissonant user can find reason to carry a daiklave made of the stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:04:03-07:00","id":1207090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1207051#post1207051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <i>had</i> the idea, though, right there in your previous sentence. You can draw forth power from soulsteel. Only two of the Exalt types we know about from the time were Dissonant with it, and even a Dissonant user can find reason to carry a daiklave made of the stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Adamant?<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted should be resonant with it like everything else, Dragon-Blooded should be neutral, and Sidereal Exalted might conceivably be neutral but at worst wouldn't be any more dissonant with it than anything else. So in those regards it wouldn't be different from orichalcum or moonsilver.<br /> <br /> As for the Lunar Exalted, it's possibly the only material they might be dissonant with, but that shouldn't be a factor against considering it &quot;one of the Magical Materials&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:36:37-07:00","id":1207105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1207090#post1207090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Adamant?<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted should be resonant with it like everything else, Dragon-Blooded should be neutral, and Sidereal Exalted might conceivably be neutral but at worst wouldn't be any more dissonant with it than anything else. So in those regards it wouldn't be different from orichalcum or moonsilver.<br /> <br /> As for the Lunar Exalted, it's possibly the only material they might be dissonant with, but that shouldn't be a factor against considering it &quot;one of the Magical Materials&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Hypothetically, you can build a daiklave out of Frozen Lightning and Demon Bamboo and a Solar should have zero problems drawing Evocations from it, but those aren't in the Five MMs because none of the other members of the Exalted Host Resonated with it. Neither Adamant nor Soulsteel have a resonant member of the original host that we know of, so Soulsteel's inclusion in the 5MMs is strange, honestly.<br /> <br /> Possibly we can blame the Necromancers for it, I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:35:24-07:00","id":1207125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1207090#post1207090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Adamant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows? Maybe adamant was not as available in Creation as the screaming ghost-metal?<br /> <br /> Or, just bear with me here, maybe no one tried to make a daiklave primarily out of adamant during the First Age?<br /> <br /> Or even possibly, the Exalted of the First Age stopped after five, even after finding good candidates for addition to the list? After all, if we can decide that Puerto Rico doesn't get to be the 51st State, I think it's entirely reasonable for Solars to like the sound of &quot;five magic materials&quot; over having to revise the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-14-2018, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:47:02-07:00","id":1207131,"title":"","content":"My personal theory is that Soulsteel opens up many themes and powers that no other MM gives access too, such as blood-based evocations, necromancy, ghosts, etc. Adamant seems a bit more limited in that aspect, with many things it could do also overlapping with other materials, so there was less of a need to use the rare Adamant in large amounts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T20:12:51-07:00","id":1207138,"title":"","content":"Abyssals were described in the core book. Soulsteel is aligned with the dead, and Deathlords are an established threat. Both are antagonists we see from day 1. Their material has to be described, it's as present a material as all others, while adamant is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-15-2018, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T00:21:32-07:00","id":1207567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1207131#post1207131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal theory is that Soulsteel opens up many themes and powers that no other MM gives access too, such as blood-based evocations, necromancy, ghosts, etc. Adamant seems a bit more limited in that aspect, with many things it could do also overlapping with other materials, so there was less of a need to use the rare Adamant in large amounts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying Soulsteel helps you find your worth in the waking world? Great, now I have <i>another</i> character I have to stat up...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>dodgemainmeleeartifactstarmetalflamepiece,retainer 3, demesne4, craft:alchemy,awareness,TCS....</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T01:02:16-07:00","id":1207575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1207567#post1207567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're saying Soulsteel helps you find your worth in the waking world? Great, now I have <i>another</i> character I have to stat up...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>dodgemainmeleeartifactstarmetalflamepiece,retainer 3, demesne4, craft:alchemy,awareness,TCS....</i></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yarhnam as a Shadowlands in the midst of a Pupeteer's Plague is a beautiful, beautiful thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T04:51:23-07:00","id":1207606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1207567#post1207567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're saying Soulsteel helps you find your worth in the waking world?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh indeed, I remember that one time I went to have certain medical tests done, they stuck a tube and needle in my arm, goddamn werewolf popped out. Unbelievably embarrassing.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for soulsteel, I'd say the most likely reason that it's considered a magical material is that it's resonant with a core group of Exalted, and it would kind of suck if it was the only material that had hardly any Artifacts without a storied lineage, so they figured out that it was something up there with your jade and moonsilver and the like in the First Age because of reasons. Maybe those reasons become a bit shaky if you give them too much scrutiny, but come on, what's the point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-16-2018, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T04:59:03-07:00","id":1207608,"title":"","content":"Plus now 7/8 of the celestials get second circle necromancy, which soulsteel resonates with. That might have pushed its use up in the first age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T07:02:51-07:00","id":1207971,"title":"","content":"Finally I have reached the Artifact chapter, aaaaand I refuse to read the fiction. I mean, if you have a boyfriend and discover on his phone a bunch of pictures where he's holding hands happily with another woman, you would be angry too, right?<br /> <br /> So the first Artifact is Courate and Galliard, is it me or is the font really hard to read?<br /> <br /> Well, the backstory is pretty basic, not sure if there are even any plothooks in there. Though I kinda wonder if there are any male matchmaker/Bluesid, since female Joybringer who is also a shipper is just so cliche in 2018.<br /> <br /> Now for the mechanic. Oooooooh, weapons that encourage paired fighting is very interesting. Since I have always wanted to do a Two Swords As One (\u53cc\u5251\u5408\u58c1) martial art in Exalted, there are just so many aesthetic to draw from, the most obvious one is the yuanyang bird, or the idiom &quot;Ch\u1eafp c\u00e1nh Li\u1ec1n c\u00e0nh&quot; which is about mythological birds who can't fly without its mate and trees with intertwined branches. You can also go full gay with Black Bride White Bride style, fun with funeral and wedding for everyone!<br /> <br /> Lovers in wuxia novel are often fighting in pair when they are at maximum LOOOOVE too.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/fNF4ALN.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How I wish to have a duet battle stance with Demetheus so much right now looking at this picture (\u2565\ufe4f\u2565) This despair is turning me an Abyssal, just need to find some black make-up and spiky leather pant first.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, usually in wuxia TV show, when two characters whip out this stance it usually involves raining swordstrikes endlessly at the opponent, but Courate and gal provides a more defensive bonus. Well, I'm still at the attunement bonus so far, maybe the Charm will help more with attacking?<br /> <br /> Oh my glob, Shared-Battle Instinct's Resonance effect is so amazing at providing stunt fodders. I'm Jen so it obviously involves two bears synchronized posing at the start of battle ~&lt;3<br /> <br /> Sparks Fly Together and Celestial Union of Blades are good too. But I can't think of any examples in my head at the moment.<br /> <br /> The capstone charm, I thought Electrum sounds really weird so I search for it, turn out it's the term for a combination of gold and silver, pretty interesting since I thought it's related to........electricity at first. The effect is amazing of course, apparently this kind of fusion is a pretty popular kink with some gay men (and probably lesbian too looking at Steven Universe).<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion: </b>I have a very good impression with these two swords, anything that reminds me of wuxia battle and gay is good in my book. I may as well ditch the whole rating thing if the rest of the Artifacts are just as good as this, or else I'm gonna run out of FIVE JEN!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bHZIxaW.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-17-2018, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T09:47:00-07:00","id":1208028,"title":"","content":"I like that the picture with those two swords has two guys fighting together too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:01:28-07:00","id":1208045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1207971#post1207971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Electrum sounds really weird so I search for it, turn out it's the term for a combination of gold and silver, pretty interesting since I thought it's related to........electricity at first.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt actually is, after a fashion; electrum is close to the ancient Greek term for amber, owing to them having a similar colour, and because amber was the first material to show electrostatic properties, the ancient Greek term for it was used as the basis for terms such as electron and electricity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:49:18-07:00","id":1208061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208028#post1208028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that the picture with those two swords has two guys fighting together too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea, but the picture is kinda average for me, maybe I just watch too much gay art and is now too picky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208045#post1208045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt actually is, after a fashion; electrum is close to the ancient Greek term for amber, owing to them having a similar colour, and because amber was the first material to show electrostatic properties, the ancient Greek term for it was used as the basis for terms such as electron and electricity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, you learn something new everyday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:46:17-07:00","id":1208115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208061#post1208061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea, but the picture is kinda average for me, maybe I just watch too much gay art and is now too picky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah it really is average. It got rather cheesy, which breaks its impact a bit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T07:55:38-07:00","id":1208447,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I kinda wonder if it's possible to do a paired weapons designed to use by multi characters like this using a different MM from Orichaclum/Moonsilver?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208115#post1208115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah it really is average. It got rather cheesy, which breaks its impact a bit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would have prefer if they are in a middle of an attack or doing those wuxia lover stance. It looks a little stiff right now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:00:27-07:00","id":1208450,"title":"","content":"Jade probably works well with jade, drawing resonance from their common nature, whereas the moonsilver/orichalcum pairing is more about how the essences aligned with the sun and the moon are foils to each other.<br /> <br /> Starmetal would probably be its own thing, although its own thing can very much include blessings and curses to your allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-18-2018, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:05:25-07:00","id":1208453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208447#post1208447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I kinda wonder if it's possible to do a paired weapons designed to use by multi characters like this using a different MM from Orichaclum/Moonsilver?</div> </div> </div> </div>The five colors of jade for five companion weapons seems a good bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:06:13-07:00","id":1208454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208447#post1208447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I kinda wonder if it's possible to do a paired weapons designed to use by multi characters like this using a different MM from Orichaclum/Moonsilver?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say so. Different colours of jade, for one. Several starmetal weapons with a kind of linked destiny. I'd say that orichalcum and moonsilver take to it quite readily, and especially with this kind of partnership, but one could manage just about any combination of materials that could form <i>some</i> kind of linked use.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, now I'm picturing a soulsteel daiklave with a kind of dominating relationship to a set of Artifacts, owing to how their wielders fought in ancient times and the soulsteel overcame the others in a manner so extreme that it gained a mastery. It wouldn't be a default power of the daiklave, more something particular to that situation that was so legendary that it altered the paths along which all of the involved Artifacts develop Evocations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T09:26:04-07:00","id":1208474,"title":"","content":"Making an N/A artifact in the form of a small, plain orichalcum ring is always fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:28:18-07:00","id":1208576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208474#post1208474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making an N/A artifact in the form of a small, plain orichalcum ring is always fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>A wielder awakens its first Evocation, Willful Finger Finder, for no experience cost when she first attunes Isildur's Bane. Beings who develop an Intimacy of at least Major intensity to Isildur's Bane also unlock Precious Possession Declaration for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:42:02-07:00","id":1208582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208576#post1208576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wielder awakens its first Evocation, Willful Finger Finder, for no experience cost when she first attunes Isildur's Bane. Beings who develop an Intimacy of at least Major intensity to Isildur's Bane also unlock Precious Possession Declaration for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or its slightly more indirect reference name: Numenor's Numinous Nuisance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T17:06:15-07:00","id":1208628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1208474#post1208474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making an N/A artifact in the form of a small, plain orichalcum ring is always fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHeh, it's funny how different magical powers, and devices that carry them, can carry different weight depending on the setting.<br /> <br /> In The Lord of the Rings, the One Ring is the biggest deal ever for reasons that are... kind of nebulous in the story itself, and important primarily because of the backstory. As in, the main power of the One is that it allows one to command the will of wielders of the other Rings, and in the time of the main story that's not exactly the big threat that it used to be; by the time of the narrative's events, Sauron is actually the one holding most of the Rings, and the elves wouldn't actually wear theirs if he got the One back anyway. Having it would let implicitly let Sauron have a certain degree of power over elven havens that have been sustained by their Rings, such as Rivendell and Lothlorien, but he doesn't even really need those; even without his Ring, Sauron is powerful enough to overcome all opposition*. Despite what Gandalf says at the start, Sauron doesn't actually need the Ring to win out over everybody, and its importance is in the chance it affords to the good guys, literally being the only chance they've got of surviving his onslaught by destroying his body and power permanently.<br /> <br /> \u200bThose narrative elements are... kind of hard to carry over to Exalted (not least in terms of figuring out how to transform them into discrete and comprehensible powers), and even once they get there they don't carry as much weight. I would say that generally, the One Ring might be translated as having certain mind control powers, which would probably make it level 5 or even 4, unless one opted to translate some of its concept as something like the Ebon Dragon's Wedding Ring, where it kind of made the wearer into an extension of one of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> \u200b* Tolkien once noted in a letter to friends that even if another person got the One Ring, unless they were Gandalf, Sauron would remain personally powerful enough to take it from that person by force if he needed to go do it personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T08:42:20-07:00","id":1221163,"title":"","content":"I was trapped in no-Wifi land for these past few weeks while surrounded by hot bears 24/7 so there is a lot of repressed Jenergy here. If the next Artifact isn't good there is a very good chance that I'll explode into a shower of rainbow.<br /> <br /> So the next one is called...um.....This staff? Wait, according to Google it's actually another name for, eh, that pointy weaver thing which screws over Briar Rose in Sleeping Beauty, a spindle going by online dictionary. I hope that I'm not the only one who doesn't know what a distaff is............<br /> <br /> Heeey, the backstory here is super good, I love Dragonfly\u2019s first effects, plus it shows how the weapon\u2019s personality and Evocation can change according to how it\u2019s used by their master. Plus I\u2019m a sucker for pacifist character and Aridara sounds like an amazing NPC, I kinda hope that she gonna appear in later supplement someday.<br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m curious and google Cynansure, turns out it\u2019s an actual real word and not a made-up one. Where do people manage to find these things anyway???? I guess it\u2019s one of the talents that you must have if you want to be a writer. It\u2019s also have come to my attention that I repeat words and phrases way too much, I\u2019m sorry for any discomfort that I cause to you guy m(_ _)m<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, let go to the Evocation sections ~<br /> <br /> So you can create infinity silks with the sword? I feel as though it\u2019s a giant economical disaster in waiting if this is true.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand the first Evocation is already making me so strange inside, I love Medicine artifact, but past Edition only have the Satchel of Healing which\u2026\u2026boost your dicepool or something like that, I only remember being bored to death by reading it. But this is different, the charm name give it a very distinctive aesthetic compared to \u201cYou heal good\u201d, plus the second effect is just so eye-catching.<br /> <br /> Tarantula\u2019s Grip is making me think about something, in fiction, spider-web seems to be extremely sticky only when it\u2019s used by actual spiders, you touch one and you are pretty much stuck there. Meanwhile, Spider-man\u2019s web seems like it\u2019s made from wet noodles since villain destroys and escapes from it so easily. And this Evocation makes me feel like a real spider right now instead of some teenager in red spandex, come here and give Jen some bodyjuice!<br /> <br /> Wrapped Fly Atemi, on one hand, the imagery evoked by the name is super gross, on the other hand, the effect has so much Jen potential\u2026\u2026\u2026.Do you think Distaff will like it if I only use them in the bedroom?<br /> <br /> Poppet-Knitting Practice is nice, as does Snarl-Silken Pankratiast (it mean super sexy sex between guys in Greek for the uninitiated)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/gxrcFDd.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Aaaaanyway, the capstone is so good, one of the thing that makes me despair is that Solar\u2019s Medicine have no way to deal with disease outbreaks aside from just dealing with every singled patient, I mean, you can speed it up with Medicine and Athletic charms, but it just looks super silly in my head, doctor Flash zapping around the city curing people may sounds awesome to other people, but it\u2019s just not a thing for me. But the Silken Army solve that problem beautifully, having a big Red Cross staffs on demands is very very nice indeed, too bad it\u2019s only once per story :\u2019(((<br /> <br /> Finally, for the \u201ccapstone\u201d, I will repeat what I say with Wrapped Fly Atemi, do you think Distaff will like it if I only use them in the bedroom?<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Good backstory, good Evocations, there are so many different effects enhancing different Abilities, and yet there isn't a sense of them being jammed together for no reasons while I was reading them, some of the Evocations also gives me inspiration for non-combat Evocation as well, plus there are some very good Jen in there. Distaff, you are a true hunk in my heart!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bHZIxaW.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T09:01:02-07:00","id":1221167,"title":"","content":"Ahh, I missed this thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221163#post1221163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the next one is called...um.....This staff? Wait, according to Google it's actually another name for, eh, that pointy weaver thing which screws over Briar Rose in Sleeping Beauty, a spindle going by online dictionary. I hope that I'm not the only one who doesn't know what a distaff is............</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHuh; I'm suddenly thinking that it may be that the reason I even know what a distaff is is because I looked into a bunch of things about textile manufacturing after watching Kill la Kill.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr maybe it was just after one of those times I read about the importance it had to Medieval economies...<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, the distaff is actually a distinct tool from the spindle, although they are used in conjunction; the distaff is the rod on which one holds a bundle of the raw material, such as a big clump of wool, and the spindle is a smaller rod that is used to draw away the fibres as individual threads.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T09:54:50-07:00","id":1221187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221167#post1221167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnyway, the distaff is actually a distinct tool from the spindle, although they are used in conjunction; the distaff is the rod on which one holds a bundle of the raw material, such as a big clump of wool, and the spindle is a smaller rod that is used to draw away the fibres as individual threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh I learn something everyday, not sure if I'm not searching hard enough, but it seems like distaff is an Europe tool only, since people just harvest the silk <a href=\"https://1.bp.blogspot.com/-gB2Td__Igys/VZpVo1ycPeI/AAAAAAAABy4/SS4sFaj3XhE/s400/soi-tam.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">directly </a>from the silkworm or just not <a href=\"http://dangcongsan.vn/DATA/Upload/News/2015/3/X%C6%AF%20LANH%20DET%20VAI%2016.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">using </a>a distaff-like for weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T12:19:24-07:00","id":1221234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221167#post1221167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, I missed this thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't even realize how much I missed it 'till I saw Jen posting in it again.<br /> <br /> Glad to see you cover my consistently-favorite Artifact, Jen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Also, while it's true that the ability to produce arbitrary amounts of silk in any color <i>can</i> play hob with economies, I'd argue that absent a shitload of Craft Charms <i>and</i> an infrastructure capable of transporting his goods across vast distances, a given Exalt is likely to only have a <i>big</i> impact on the markets of a few cities.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-22-2018, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T16:14:23-07:00","id":1221294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221234#post1221234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't even realize how much I missed it 'till I saw Jen posting in it again.<br /> <br /> Glad to see you cover my consistently-favorite Artifact, Jen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Also, while it's true that the ability to produce arbitrary amounts of silk in any color <i>can</i> play hob with economies, I'd argue that absent a shitload of Craft Charms <i>and</i> an infrastructure capable of transporting his goods across vast distances, a given Exalt is likely to only have a <i>big</i> impact on the markets of a few cities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what you\u2019re saying is that a Solar with the Distaff could partner with the Guild to monopolize silk manufacturing all over Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T17:23:43-07:00","id":1221315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221294#post1221294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Solar with the Distaff could partner with the Guild to monopolize silk manufacturing all over Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm reminded of one book commenting that it's difficult for the Guild to get in on the drug trade in some place or another, owing to the fact that drugs grow in people's back gardens.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is to say, even if there <i>was</i> practicality to having one's entire supply of silk dependent on a single Exalt doing nothing but draw it from their sword forever (which seems to have flaws in the area of them actually doing that, and what the rate of production is), it's going to be hard to eliminate competition of silkworms continue existing, and are right there.<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, it's my understanding that the value of silk has generally been in quality and beauty, rather than functional scarcity, and that in lands to which it is native, that would often be maintained by sumptuary laws.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus, if we go by certain modern economic practices, I can readily see somebody in possession of a large supply of silk with minimal overhead going &quot;hey, now I can stockpile this stuff and regularly dole it out in small quantities at the current market value indefinitely&quot;. Just like the modern diamond market.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I'm mostly inclined to think that the Distaff does not produce quantities at a high enough rate to dramatically affect the supply, even if one did want to tell a story of undermining state financial systems based on the manufacturing of silk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T17:33:53-07:00","id":1221322,"title":"","content":"My actual plan was \u201cuse the solar to flood the market, drive down the price of silk until it\u2019s unsustainable, aquire enough of the silk producing villages that you just put out of business so that you\u2019re not dependent on the solar later, and then, once you own everything, wait a year or two to ensure that silkworms not owned by you die out, then start restricting the supply and make your actual profit.\u201d<br /> <br /> That said, I don\u2019t necessarily know how well it would work in practice. You make a good point about sumptuary laws and silk lasts pretty well too, so once the bottom drops out of the market it might take decades to recover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T18:03:15-07:00","id":1221333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221322#post1221322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aquire enough of the silk producing villages that you just put out of business</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's my understanding that historically, peasant silk farmers didn't make that stuff to turn a profit, they did it to have the cash reserves to pay their taxes.<br /> <br /> \u200bTaxes that were set at rates and in currency specifically for the sake of incentivizing farmers to devote time to cultivating silk.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat does it mean for Guild merchants to acquire silk manufacturers during a period when they're not effectively producing silk?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">wait a year or two to ensure that silkworms not owned by you die out</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, I was going to make a comment on how, in the absence of a silk market, more of the worms would survive owing to not being boiled for the textile, but I had the sense to actually read into it and find how the kind of domestication that makes them worthwhile for human purposes basically destroyed their capacity to survive and propagate on their own; in the absence of an incentive to have them, they really would die out within a generation owing to their inability to breed without assistance, not to mention how many would be eaten as a result of things like being unable to fly, or camouflage, or have an instinctual fear of predators.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Distaff could manage it on its own, but I've wondered before about wedding certain kinds of Artifact to sorcerous workings.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T22:13:34-07:00","id":1221382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221315#post1221315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and that in lands to which it is native</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I just read something a month ago about how silkworm aren't native to Europe and Rome have to import silk from China, it takes hundred of years later into the Byzantine period with the emperor's sponsor that silkworm are finally smuggled into Europe.<br /> <br /> I can see it now, the Circle travel to a citystate where silk are imported and they get kidnapped by the local king to be his personal silk producer, too bad the Zenith is just so hot and cute that king goes &quot;I thought I want the ivory thread of the worm, but all I really want is your hand in marriage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hurrgh, this weapon is even more Jen than I have thought! Truly a formidable hunk indeed.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T23:08:46-07:00","id":1221393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1221382#post1221382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh, I just read something a month ago about how silkworm aren't native to Europe and Rome have to import silk from China, it takes hundred of years later into the Byzantine period with the emperor's sponsor that silkworm are finally smuggled into Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The coffee bean has a similar, albeit possibly more gruesome, history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T21:42:52-07:00","id":1221614,"title":"","content":"One of the fun aspects of Creation is that you can take the whole concept of silkworm smuggling and reimagine it as giant silk producing spider smuggling (though you might want the silk spiders to be more the size of large tomatoes instead of horses, if you're planning on actually smuggling them. I think stealing Halta's giant riding spiders counts as &quot;rustling&quot; instead of smuggling.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:49:30-07:00","id":1223244,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Fists of Titan, which immediately get a negative point for tricking me into thinking it will be a punchy enhancer, but it back to normal now, I\u2019m Jen, I can\u2019t say no to Grand Goremaul.<br /> Aaaah yesssss, a monstrosity that stands taller than most men, that description right there is enough to give this a beefcake rating, I\u2019M NOT BIASED, well, maybe I am, but only toward huge weapons.<br /> <br /> The weapon\u2019s backstory\u2026..eeeeeeeh\u2026\u2026I have to wonder if Exalted player usually named their characters using title or real name, I mostly use the latter since I like researching other cultures, plus using the former result in\u2026.this. I have to read the paragraph 3 times to understand who\u2019s who, so basically during the Divine Revolution, there is an Exigent who is the student of Pasiap, they forge FoT which is then used by the Nameless Hero lady to defeat Kirby Cave, wait, is her name Nameless Hero or Nameless Hero of the Divine Revolution???<br /> <br /> It\u2019s all too confusing, using real names is much better for me, plus you can kinda envision how a character looks from their name alone I think, for example someone named Demetheus probably pranking around the South with only a chlamys on his body, or a super tight muscle cuirass, riiiiiiight? It is not, Demetheus is actually fully clothed\u2026..<br /> <br /> The night is long and cold, to walk through it without a picture of stupid sexy shirtless Demetheus as protection is absolute despair.<br /> <br /> Oookay, it seems like FoS\u2019s gimmick is Aiming for Charge to be used, which is pretty interesting since Aiming is pretty much tied to the hip with ranged weapons in\u2026.pretty much every media works that I have seen, if it does appear with a melee weapon the latter will be something like a rapier or something. To see someone Aiming with a GIGANTIC MAGIC HAMMER is pretty refreshing.<br /> Mammoth Slam Quake is an AoE shockwave attack, and now I\u2019m sad that there is now shockwave charm for Solar Brawl and Melee. Since everyone is knock down If they fail the roll, a FoT user will be very good friend with a Tiger stylist I think, well, as long as the Tiger have wings so they don\u2019t get affected by Mammoth Slam. And now I suddenly remember about a character in Investiture of the Gods, Huang Feihu i.e Golden Flying Tiger who looks so so very <a href=\"http://p1.qhimg.com/t0162ad7cded25f8157.png\" target=\"_blank\">hawt</a>.<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Hammering Blow gives you a bonus for making smashing attack, so this is an example of making Evocations that guide the player toward a specific playstyle. Ooooh, I can already think of so many different effects in the same vein as UHB.<br /> <br /> Finally some smashy smashy with Bone Crushing Strike. Hmmm, I have always puzzled, if an effect like disease or crippling says that it needs to be cured with magic, can a roll enhanced with Excellency be sufficient, or do I need a specific charm for that.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: I think I\u2019m gonna wrap it up now, the weapon is good, but for some reasons I just don\u2019t have much to say about the thing, it feels kindaaaa vanilla, which is sad since this is the first Grand Goremau\u2026\u2026Oh no, it\u2019s the only Grand Goremaul in the book according to the bookmark\u2026\u2026.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I have to give Fist of Titan NO JEN! He\u2019s just not that hot for me, how can a Grand Goremaul be unsexy to me huh??!!!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QLh7D8z.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-01-2018, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T15:36:22-07:00","id":1223746,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t worry, there\u2019s a set of smashfists in there a bit later that you might like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T04:54:36-07:00","id":1223881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l