mber","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T05:50:08-07:00","id":1223894,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223882#post1223882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was one but it got cut, apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bIf I told 'em once, I told 'em a thousand times; you grasp it handle first!</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223884#post1223884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the connection is obvious, but I'm really into Artifact scythe whose theme isn't all doom-and-gloom or MAXIMUM-UNDEAD-AND-MURDER!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I once had an idea for an orichalcum grimscythe, but I never wrote it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T08:22:11-07:00","id":1223916,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I'm searching the Internet for example Grand Grimscythe, it seems like most of them are limited to either plant, harvest or death themes. I didn't realize how scythe have such a strong and defined grip on people imagination like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223886#post1223886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if its love of doomed things is akin to that of your precious Ebon Dragon? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Grand Grimscythe with spider-lily/poppy imagery would be super nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223894#post1223894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I once had an idea for an orichalcum grimscythe, but I never wrote it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, what is its theme? I want to create an orichaclum grand grimscythe too, but I still have trouble distancing myself from creating a reaping tool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-01-2018, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T09:03:04-07:00","id":1223922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223916#post1223916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Oooh, what is its theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo, I mean that not writing anything down means that I don't remember anything about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T11:04:43-07:00","id":1223960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223922#post1223922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I mean that not writing anything down means that I don't remember anything about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That just means we have to <i>re</i>create it. Fire up the factory-cathedral! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T11:50:09-07:00","id":1223971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223916#post1223916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh, what is its theme? I want to create an orichaclum grand grimscythe too, but I still have trouble distancing myself from creating a reaping tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scythes are very purpose built after all...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T13:03:21-07:00","id":1223981,"title":"","content":"To serve as a functional weapon, a scythe really needs it's blade flipped 90 degrees so it sticks straight out. <br /> <br /> The problem is, this doesn't look as badass.<br /> <br /> My proposed solution is to make a scythe with a blade that rotates when you swing it, fusing functionality with aesthetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T13:39:03-07:00","id":1223990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223981#post1223981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To serve as a functional weapon, a scythe really needs it's blade flipped 90 degrees so it sticks straight out. <br /> <br /> The problem is, this doesn't look as badass.<br /> <br /> My proposed solution is to make a scythe with a blade that rotates when you swing it, fusing functionality with aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons I forgave and fell in love with Crescent Rose.<br /> <br /> It can be used in \u201ctraditional\u201d form for hooking and guillotine chops, or extended to act like an actual war-scythe. She rarely does the later, but I can pretend she does it more often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T14:14:28-07:00","id":1223995,"title":"","content":"Well, if the scythe end doesn't dip down too far, it is closer to a dagger-axe.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger-axe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Dagger_axe_with_engraved_decoration_of_a_tiger%2C_China%2C_Warring_States_period%2C_475-221_BC%2C_bronze_-_%C3%96stasiatiska_museet%2C_Stockholm_-_DSC09554.JPG/1280px-Dagger_axe_with_engraved_decoration_of_a_tiger%2C_China%2C_Warring_States_period%2C_475-221_BC%2C_bronze_-_%C3%96stasiatiska_museet%2C_Stockholm_-_DSC09554.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger-axe\" target=\"_blank\"> Dagger-axe - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger-axe\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger-axe </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T17:25:16-07:00","id":1224031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223995#post1223995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if the scythe end doesn't dip down too far, it is closer to a dagger-axe.<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger-axe\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger-axe</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Practically, Ruby <i>is</i> using it like an axe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T18:16:43-07:00","id":1224038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1223981#post1223981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To serve as a functional weapon, a scythe really needs it's blade flipped 90 degrees so it sticks straight out.<br /> <br /> The problem is, this doesn't look as badass.<br /> <br /> My proposed solution is to make a scythe with a blade that rotates when you swing it, fusing functionality with aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even mounted on a conventional pole, a scythe-blade makes a for a pretty poor excuse for a glaive. Too light &amp; thin to be a decent polearm; just because we have a treatise for fighting with them <a href=\"http://wiktenauer.com/wiki/Paulus_Hector_Mair\" target=\"_blank\">http://wiktenauer.com/wiki/Paulus_Hector_Mair</a> doesn't mean it's anything more than a gimmick. It's exactly the same as trying to use a whipper-snipper to murder people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T23:53:59-07:00","id":1224094,"title":"","content":"So I re-read Fists of Titan again, maybe it'll be interesting this time....well, it still doesn't evoke any Jen in me. Buuuuut, I just noticed one of the latter charm can manipulate.....gravity? Turns out white jade can have Evocation with gravity theme.<br /> <br /> Isn't that word, or power, felt a little modern? Since I only encounter them in sci-fi or comic book so seeing such a thing in a fantasy setting is a little weird.<br /> <br /> And if white jade can control gravity, should Moonsilver and Orichaclum have them too, since they are gigantic ball of mass after all (which may not be true in Ex3, but still....)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T00:07:16-07:00","id":1224099,"title":"","content":"The word &quot;gravity&quot; is hundreds of years old, actually. It basically just referred to something being very heavy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T03:56:24-07:00","id":1224127,"title":"","content":"The nice thing about artifacts is you basically take the abstract concept of &quot;this is an effective weapon&quot; and hammer it into the metal. So they can look however you like and still work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T07:17:19-07:00","id":1224151,"title":"","content":"I like Fist of the Titans. Especially its doom-combo.<br /> <br /> The doom-combo is using Chamber Fist Charge (preferably two purchases of such, so that you only have to do it once) to build up to Titanic Fist Devastation, which can trigger a reflexive Mammoth Slam Quake (which benefits from the Charges spent on TFD), which allows the reflexive activation of Crater-Gouging Blow (which benefits from the Charges spent on TFD). Each of these earth-elemental Evocations chains into each other, and all are built around the hammer's defining mechanic.<br /> <br /> It's beautiful, and you could technically do it every other turn (if you're a Solar or Dragon-Blood with the Charge repurchase), but it costs you a minimum of 14m, 1wp, and 3i every time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something that bothers me about Fist of the Titans is that it was printed out before a non-elemental, hammer-centric martial art Style.<br /> <br /> It's a white jade hammer very much based around earth elementalism, but it has non-earth elemental Evocations that seem like they could have been non-elemental hammer Charms; Unstoppable Hammering Blow, Bone-Crushing Strike, Colossal Whirling Strike...<br /> <br /> Bone-Crushing Strike and Colossal Whirling Strike are also notable in being Charms that don't necessarily play into the Fist's unique Charge mechanic or its doom-combo, despite serving as gateways to the capstone of that combo. But as I'll explain, they do serve purposes...<br /> <br /> <br /> Unstoppable Hammering Blow seems to interact with Titanic Fist Devastation, which is perhaps enough of a smashing attack to benefit from the +1 accuracy, though it doesn't seem to need the Defense penalty waiver. The Evocation can even be gained for free. It definitely fits and helps with the weapon's emphasis on smashing attacks, but so would the kind of hammer Martial Art Style I'd like to see. It does not involve the Charge mechanic at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bone-Crushing Strike can also supplement Titanic Fist Devastation. But it doesn't synergize with the doom-combo. In fact, in some ways, it seems to interfere.<br /> <br /> Titanic Fist Devastation cannot trigger Mammoth Slam Quake without causing at least three levels of damage, and Bone-Crushing Strike trades away a level of damage to inflict a crippling penalty. Maybe that health level stills counts, but one of the Evocations should explicitly clarify the matter.<br /> <br /> More arguably worse, the crippling penalty doesn't make someone more vulnerable to Mammoth Slam Quake, which seems like a wasted opportunity. The entire weapon is building towards Titanic Fist Devastation and half of the doom-combo hinges on Mammoth Slam Quake succeeding in rendering your victims prone.<br /> <br /> Also, since Bone-Crushing Strike requires one Charge to use, it competes with Titanic Fist Devastation for Charges.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the doom-combo is expensive, and using Bone-Crushing Strike against a dueling opponent or the most dangerous of multiple opponents at the beginning of a fight could really help survive Charging up every other turn for the rest of the fight (since it penalizes attack pools) or help keep an opponent from disengaging (since you can't Rush and Aim at the same time). Leaving yourself with an odd number of Charges also points to Avalanche Hammer Attack and Colossal Whirling Strike.<br /> <br /> Having 3+ Charges for later also lets you use Bone-Crushing Strike later on your target for TFD, which might not necessarily be the target of the initial Bone-Crushing Strike. Or else that target might have used Anathema devilry to avoid or remove the crippling penalty.<br /> <br /> Maybe an upgrade following Titanic Fist Devastation could apply the crippling penalty of Bone-Crushing Strike to the opposed roll of Mammoth Slam Quake.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colossal Whirling Strike is so much fun that I ask why it should be given to one specific hammer.<br /> <br /> The previously mentioned possible upgrade to Bone-Crushing Strike would also serve as an upgrade to this Evocation, since its reset condition requires beating a significant opponent's opposed roll with Mammoth Slam Quake.<br /> <br /> However, Colossal Whirling Strike doesn't properly synergize with the doom-combo. Oh, the damage bonus to Titanic Fist Devastation is definitely important, but knocking your target out to medium range removes them from the radius of Mammoth Slam Quake, and thus also prevents them from being a valid target of Crater-Gouging Blow.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, using Colossal Whirling Strike can be very useful for buying yourself time to build up Charges.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem worthwhile to combo Bone-Crushing Strike and Colossal Whirling Strike together, though. There's little point to using BCS twice against the same opponent (and would running out of Charge after the first invocation exempt you from paying the mote cost of the second invocation?), and if you're going to be standing around Charging up, your opponent doesn't need to succeed at Rush actions. But they might have those particular Rush Charms that immediately close gaps, and you might decide to tactically retreat instead of Charging up.<br /> <br /> <i><b>EDIT:</b> Colossal Whirling Strike isn't two separate attack rolls; it's mechanically a single attack. You wouldn't invoke or pay for Bone-Crushing Strike twice.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> So, all in all, it's a very lovely hammer. Especially if you have someone protecting you while you Charge.<br /> <br /> Ah, it's worth mentioning that Chambered Fist Charge very much does count as an Aim action, so while it might seem like a poor man's Strength-Increasing Exercise, it definitely offers a unique advantage towards immediately attacking someone after using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-02-2018, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T14:04:44-07:00","id":1224230,"title":"","content":"<i>EDIT: Got too far ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> Robert confirmed that Mammoth Slam Quake requires an addition three Charges to extend its range, separate from the variable Charge cost to activate the Charm and intensify its effect.<br /> <br /> Also that the health level sacrificed to Bone-Crushing Strike does not count towards the minimum necessary to trigger a reflexive Mammoth Slam Quake with Titanic Fist Devastation.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> One of the most powerful, internal combinations with Fist of the Titans is to spend at least four turns building up eight points of Charge, and then unleash a single attack of Titanic Fist Devastation with at least three charges behind it, but no more than five.<br /> <br /> Unstoppable Hammering Blow adds a non-Charm dice to the attack dice-pool.<br /> <br /> Solar-exclusive Avalanche Hammer Attack triggers as long as the hammer has at least three points of Charge; it doesn't spend them. The Solar can spend 3m to use Rising Sun Slash without using a full Melee Excellency.<br /> <br /> Colossal Whirling Strike adds dice of bonus damage and knocks the target out to medium range.<br /> <br /> If you spent four rather than five points of Charge on Titanic Fist Devastation, you can pay for Bone-Crushing Strike. Beware that the health level you trade away for the crippling penalty does not count towards the necessary minimum!<br /> <br /> If you inflicted at least three levels of damage, a reflexive Mammoth Slam Quake can ride the variable number of Charges you spent on Titanic Fist Devastation, but now you need to spend another three Charges to extend its range out to medium, catching the target of Colossal Whirling Strike (and anyone else in the radius).<br /> <br /> Successfully knocking over any significant opponent in that radius resets Colossal Whirling Strike AND allows you to trigger Crater-Gouging Blow, helping you recover a bit of Initiative after being reset to base.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a beautiful, brutal machine of smashing, in the hands of a Resonant master.<br /> <br /> You actually use just about EVERY single Evocation within a single round, all against the same target, though it takes a long time to set up. Could be worth it if you have a friend with solid Defend Other capability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-02-2018, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T08:38:02-07:00","id":1228865,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty happy that this read-through is really helping me learn new words since I didn\u2019t know what a knuckle is until now.<br /> <br /> The art here is good, very dynamic. Though it still not quite outrageous enough for me, still felt a bit too generic, like, you can place it in another fantasy gameline and nobody would notice that this is art from Exalted. I probably just gonna stop commenting on the art from now on, I feel like I'm complaining too much and it's not really fun at all.<br /> <br /> So, this is Frost-Thorn Knuckles, which is made from Moonsilver instead of Blue Jade? Sooo the material all comes from the North so it\u2019s not that unreasonable, also, in East Asian (or just Chinese?), the Moon is can sometimes be called Supreme Yin (\u592a\u9670), and Yin is all about coldness so I\u2019m not quite surprised when moon-theme things also has ice in it powerset, I mean, sun-theme artifacts usually involve shooting hot flame as its main schtick, so why can\u2019t moon artifacts shoots moon ice :\u2019D<br /> <br /> Though I\u2019m a little curious if there is anything else in the book that is similar to Frost-Thorn, a quick skim and there is a Green Jade sword with Red Jade theme and Orichalcum sword with Blue Jade theme.<br /> <br /> I think that my preferred way to approach this kind of Artifact is using the Impossible Creatures (IC) method instead of a lego one, so basically IC is some really old game where you can combine animal\u2019s part into chimera i.e Flying Dogotus with Batwing and Wasp Stinger can be a real thing. And the game doesn\u2019t really say \u201cYou can\u2019t combine this part with this part\u201d, as opposed to lego where piece X need to be correctly connected to piece A, it\u2019s kinda the same with making Artifact in Exalted, as long as there is some kind of \u201cglue\u201d that binds or connect the theme together, I\u2019m fine with things like Storm Caller and Burning Branch, it opens up some very interesting themes for Evocation, like, a Soulsteel sword being able to create burning black flame since there is sealed fire elemental inside, or a living Green Jade rose being encased inside a block of magic ice allowing the user to call up blood-sucking ice rose from the ground.<br /> Oi oi, I ramble way too much, this is supposed to be about finding the perfect sword husband, not navel-gazing about Exalted!?<br /> <br /> So reading through the backstory, I\u2019m super not into the whole savage barbarian hunter Lunar thing, my eyes just kinda glaze over the whole text now. I predict an incoming No Jen rating\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> Or maaaybe not, the attunement\u2019s effect appears in the first paragraph just under the weapon\u2019s name, but the way it\u2019s written here just makes the weapon\u2026\u2026\u2026kinda sexy somehow, now I\u2019m thinking about Hugh Jackman for some reasons, why am I thinking about Hugh Jackman??!!<br /> <br /> The first three Artifacts are kinda meh in term of husband material, but Frost-Thorn is just so good, I want to draw the spirit of the Artifact now! Just imagine it, firm and strong muscle harden by the Northern wind for you to bury your face in, the head of an apex predator perfectly designed for kissing, claws of silver ice used exclusively to hold your hands through the festival...To create these dark thoughts swirling in my maiden heart, the writer of this weapon must be a disciple of Satan himself!? I have to stay strong and continue the read-through at all cost!<br /> <br /> Hey, I really like the first charm, the backstory is all kill and murder and \u201cMe Lunar Me Strok\u201d so the first effect not being combat related is pretty refreshing, it\u2019s a nice example to steal for your Artifact too, just replace tundra with swamp/desert/underwater\u2026etc. The bonus if you have specific Ability is very interesting too, like, just saying &quot;You can ignore wound penalty&quot; is suuuuper boring, but framing it as you getting a niffy extra power if you have Survival 4 make me all giddy inside.<br /> <br /> The next 2 charms are kinda vanilla, I love the image evoked by Blood-Freezing Strike though.<br /> <br /> So Fimbulwinter is a real word and it sounds super creepy, mainly because the Google search gives me a bunch of blurry pictures with people in the dark woods, I\u2019m easily scared by this type of photos, urgh, I shouldn\u2019t have look at them at night.<br /> <br /> Blizzard Claw Swipe is super wicked, I just wish that there is a way to reset it somehow, I want to shatter every limb of the enemy so much. Waaaaaaait, why does the fluff says that you impale the enemy but the charm\u2019s name is Blizzard Claw\u2026\u2026Swipe??? Oh, Google tells me that swipe can also (informally) mean strike.<br /> <br /> Aaand that\u2019s it? Having only 5 charms is kinda short, isn\u2019t it? Courante and Distaff both have 8, Fist of Titan has 9, I wonder why FTK has so few compared to the first three :\u2019o<br /> <br /> Conclusion: TERRIBLE BACKSTORY! But Frost-Thorn Knuckles' quality as a ridiculously hot boyfriend shines through all hardship, definitely would date, so take these Beefcake rating for corrupting this innocent Jen, you damn sexy beast.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bHZIxaW.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-21-2018, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T10:23:55-07:00","id":1228889,"title":"","content":"It is a great artifact somewhat lessened by an origin and backstory that does less to justify its elemental powers than most jade artifacts.<br /> <br /> Fimbulwinter isn\u2019t a world, though you probably meant to say \u201cword\u201d. I don\u2019t know what image you looked up, but it refers to a three-year-long winter which is supposed to herald Ragnarok, where the world and most everyone in it dies in a huge war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T11:00:14-07:00","id":1228905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1228889#post1228889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a great artifact somewhat lessened by an origin and backstory that does less to justify its elemental powers than most jade artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the only Moonsilver thing about it are the enviromental resistance Evocations at the moment, I\u2019m not quite sure if that\u2019s a good or bad thing thematically, but it being made from Moonsilver bumps it pretty high on my husband material list, icy wolf man is way hotter than snow man with claws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1228889#post1228889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fimbulwinter isn\u2019t a world, though you probably meant to say \u201cword\u201d. I don\u2019t know what image you looked up, but it refers to a three-year-long winter which is supposed to herald Ragnarok, where the world and most everyone in it dies in a huge war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it\u2019s supposed to be \u201cword\u201d, I can\u2019t believe I still making these basic typo.....<br /> <br /> And searching for fimbulwinter gives me grainy pictures of people in dark wood in the suggested picture bar so I closed the brower immediately....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-20-2018, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T11:19:59-07:00","id":1228912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1228905#post1228905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And searching for fimbulwinter gives me grainy pictures of people in dark wood in the suggested picture bar so I closed the brower immediately....</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes going straight to Wikipedia is better for terms like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T21:10:01-07:00","id":1229066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1228912#post1228912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes going straight to Wikipedia is better for terms like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, in short, is a harsh winter following a harsh winter where there should be spring, followed by a harsher winter where there should be summer. And from there, you will find only war.<br /> It's a prelude to ragnarok thingie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T22:10:46-07:00","id":1229083,"title":"","content":"It's morning now so I can look at those picture more clearly, apparantly the people in those creepy picture are.........a Nordic metal band with super Christian-Hell names for their songs, which kinda goes against the Norse name of the band, isn't it....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T00:26:07-07:00","id":1229102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1229083#post1229083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's morning now so I can look at those picture more clearly, apparantly the people in those creepy picture are.........a Nordic metal band with super Christian-Hell names for their songs, which kinda goes against the Norse name of the band, isn't it....</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, folks have drawn lots of parallels between the two religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T00:32:11-07:00","id":1229104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1229083#post1229083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's morning now so I can look at those picture more clearly, apparantly the people in those creepy picture are.........a Nordic metal band with super Christian-Hell names for their songs, which kinda goes against the Norse name of the band, isn't it....</div> </div> </div> </div>Well organized proslytizing monotheism (Christianity and Islam) have lumped together polytheism and devil worship for a good bulk of their histories. So it makes sense that someone invoking satanic imagery for shock value against social norms would make the same conflation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T00:58:54-07:00","id":1229110,"title":"","content":"Also, Christianity got so entrenched in the Nordic countries so quickly that all the records we have of Norse myth\u2014Thor and Odin and Ragnarok and such\u2014were actually written down by Christians who wanted to preserve the old Norse stories which, by the time anyone was writing them down, were passing out of common telling owing to nobody actually adhering to that religion anymore.<br /> <br /> (Which may explain why Loki is so inconsistently characterized and looks suspiciously like somebody took an ambiguous figure and twisted him into a devil lookalike.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:04:36-07:00","id":1232123,"title":"","content":"So a jess is a tool used in falconry, I honestly have never seen the word before. An artifact sling is called a sling of distant surprise, are there any reasons why it doesn\u2019t have a unique word like Grand Goremaul or Daiklaive, maybe that naming scheme is used just for closed range weapons???<br /> <br /> Turn out the \u201cHawk Star\u201d in the Artifact name comes from a creature, this makes me wonder about the concept of another (magical?) being given out a portion of their power for the PC to be made into an Artifact, is this something that all of them can do? Would they need to be at a certain power level and uniqueness? As in Hoa M\u1ed9ng, the Great Dreaming Flower from Yulegash can gift your artifact with a part of its power, but a random Living Armor that you summon can\u2019t?<br /> <br /> Oh, oooooh, I just realized something! They don\u2019t call it the Primordial War anymore in Ex3, its name is The War of the Gods now, since both Jess and Fist (IT\u2019S NOT SHIPPING, I\u2019m just too lazy to type out their full name) has the same Era name, and are both made when fighting \u201cthe enemies of the gods\u201d, though I\u2019m not really sure that this will stick with the fanbase since both new terms are a little handful to type out\u2026.<br /> <br /> And for some strange reason, I really like that the Artifact is called Jess in the second paragraph, I wonder if most Artifacts are sentience enough to react to being called by their nickname, not quite being able to talk, but more like \u201cYou can feel a murderous air surrounding Gorgon everytime you call him Gooooorgon-kun~&lt;3\u201d (I hate to use weeb vocabulary here, but English doesn\u2019t have many non-nobility pronounce to express what the speaker think about the listener, and since everyone here probably read manga, I figure that I just gonna go full weaboo).<br /> <br /> Ah, I thought you-you merely don\u2019t have to pay xp for the first Evocation, but turns out it actually you instantly have the first Evocation which is way nicer, even more so if that Evocation is the iconic effect of the Artifact.<br /> <br /> Doom-Gathering Arc is a veeeery evocative name, it gives me an image of your attack traveling toward the enemy, as it gets closer a certain feeling of doom-ness from the project starts to get bigger and bigger, and then BAM! You eat 10L decisive attack.<br /> <br /> Eeeeh, it\u2019s only once per scene, sooooo how easy it is for a Solar to rout a BG I wonder. I\u2019m still not sure why the charm is Simple, so expensive and has the once per scene requirement though, it doesn\u2019t look <i>that</i> strong.<br /> <br /> Falling star usually go with epic words since it\u2019s a rare and luminous occurrence, but pairing it with a mundane thing like stone makes me giggle inside.<br /> <br /> Falling Star Stone, Titan-Slaying Stone, Stone of the Corpse, Stone of the Sword, I actually really love that the word stone is repeated through half the tree, it feels very wuxia-esque where the main theme of certain style appears constantly in the technique\u2019s names, for example, Tathagata Divine Palm will have Immeasurable Buddha\u2019s Dharma, Temple-Surveying Buddha, Heavenly Buddha Descends to the Mortal Realm, The Western Heaven Welcomes the Buddha.<br /> <br /> The charm fluff for Stone of the Corpse reminds me of the Chinese idiom \u9b3c\u54ed\u795e\u865f i.e Crying Demons Weeping Gods, basically something so powerful and terrifying that they make these being cries in terror.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, Stone of the Sword is convincing me that starmetal has waaaaaaay too many themes for its Evocation, you have destiny and weird toilet-ninja stuffs, then spirit charms, not to mention the 5 houses of the Maiden which each has a slew of different themes.<br /> <br /> Is it bad that you can only see the Star Hawk in the final Evocation when the creature is in the Artifact\u2019s name itself? Not sure if I like the Evocation though, since my Zenith can already shoot flaming bird with Sorcery, and unlike Star Hawk, Brilliant Raptor can be (non-sexually) shot a lot.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: A very nice Artifact, kinda like an icy mild bubble tea in the evening, as in I actually doesn\u2019t feel any lewdness from the Evocation at all but it still makes me happy reading it. So I wouldn\u2019t date Jess or anything, but since the quality is good, I\u2019m gonna give it a score of GOOD NON-JEN THING!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/xPJN4S4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T11:32:26-07:00","id":1232188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1229083#post1229083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's morning now so I can look at those picture more clearly, apparantly the people in those creepy picture are.........a Nordic metal band with super Christian-Hell names for their songs, which kinda goes against the Norse name of the band, isn't it....</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Deep in the bowels of Norway, where every church has third degree burns&quot;...<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sZsYEGmhEbc\" data-code=\"sZsYEGmhEbc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sZsYEGmhEbc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> </span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">are there any reasons why it doesn\u2019t have a unique word like Grand Goremaul or Daiklaive, maybe that naming scheme is used just for closed range weapons</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Oh, not just close-ranged weapons; don't forget that we've got powerbows and dragon sigh wands.<br /> <br /> I think that in some cases it's just a matter of a given writer having had a difficult time thinking of something similarly brief and punchy for slings. Particularly since they're not commonly a legendary weapon, and the myths I know of in which they feature, such as David vs Goliath, their commonness and simplicity is part of the point; there's a dramatic irony to the idea that the huge scary Philistine gets taken down by the simple weapon of a shepherd.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">this makes me wonder about the concept of another (magical?) being given out a portion of their power for the PC to be made into an Artifact, is this something that all of them can do</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't see why not; Spring Razor, from the core, is made from the tooth of a defeated elemental dragon, after all.<br /> <br /> I would think that just about any spirit might be valid for such an endeavour, just with a sense that a regular god or demon probably shouldn't be providing something that is the basis for a 5-dot Artifact (barring a particularly invested relationship to involved Exalted), and that the degree to which the spirit informs the resulting item's legend should depend on how important their personality and actions are in the story of it being made. Say, if a direlash is made including hairs taken from blood apes referenced as almost a footnote, no more important than being a presumed source of slashing fibres, then the weapon's character is liable to come from somewhere else in the story. It would be different if it's a specific blood ape with whom one had a noteworthy interaction.</span></span></span></div> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T22:01:14-07:00","id":1232309,"title":"","content":"Ooh, and now I wonder if 1CD considers it a privilege to be remade into a 5-dot Artifact. I always thought being made into an object is one of the worse fate for a character, but Alveua's write-up seems to suggest that some people think that it's an awesome opportunity....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T00:38:38-07:00","id":1232326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232309#post1232309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, and now I wonder if 1CD considers it a privilege to be remade into a 5-dot Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably depends on the individual demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T05:11:30-07:00","id":1232347,"title":"","content":"A first circle might not have enough oomph in it to deserve a 5-dot. Usually that is reserved for creatures apocalyptic in their own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T05:37:06-07:00","id":1232350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232309#post1232309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, and now I wonder if 1CD considers it a privilege to be remade into a 5-dot Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't really thinking of it as remaking myself, more of an Artifact built around or including the parts of a spirit that may or may not have been slain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought being made into an object is one of the worse fate for a character, but Alveua's write-up seems to suggest that some people think that it's an awesome opportunity....</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't discount the existence of people with some unusual sensibilities, or obsessions that override their investment in their own life, but I also tended to read the idea of people going to the Forge of Night willingly as not really knowing what they were in for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232347#post1232347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A first circle might not have enough oomph in it to deserve a 5-dot. Usually that is reserved for creatures apocalyptic in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under normal circumstances, absolutely. I was thinking it would only be for one that had a really, really significant relationship with an Exalt involved in the Artifact's creation. The idea not being so much that it's powerful because of what it draws from the spirit, but because of what it personifies for the Exalt, with the components being like totemic representations of that.<br /> <br /> Mind, there's also generally been an idea that First Circle demons are capable of growing in power (which is part of how some of them become citizens), so it might not be beyond the realm of reason to have one that, over millennia, became exceptional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T05:39:52-07:00","id":1232351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232347#post1232347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A first circle might not have enough oomph in it to deserve a 5-dot. Usually that is reserved for creatures apocalyptic in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spring Razor is just three dots despite being made from a Dragon-level Wood elemental that required a sworn brotherhood of Dragon-Blooded to kill, and the Terrestrial crafter devoted a significant span of her life to creating while also using lots of other poisons and special firewood at great expense from across Creation. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a Lunar made the three-dot Frost-Thorn Knuckles without a single Air elemental or spirit being involved. The most impressive kill on the list was a tyrant lizard, with no mentioned or hinted special characteristics (such as living in the frozen North so important to the weapon, when Tyrant Lizards live in the South/Southeast).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T06:19:49-07:00","id":1232356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232351#post1232351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most impressive kill on the list was a tyrant lizard\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you might be underselling how impressive that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:39:38-07:00","id":1232368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232356#post1232356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you might be underselling how impressive that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is in comparison to a dragon-level Wood Elemental, remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:43:53-07:00","id":1232370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232347#post1232347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A first circle might not have enough oomph in it to deserve a 5-dot. Usually that is reserved for creatures apocalyptic in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the crafting rule doesn't require you to have materials from apocalyptic creature to make high rating Artifact, so I figure that it's the crafter's skill which is more important rather than the material source if you want a 5-dot daiklaive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:50:55-07:00","id":1232372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232368#post1232368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is in comparison to a dragon-level Wood Elemental, remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:13:15-07:00","id":1232384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1232351#post1232351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spring Razor is just three dots despite being made from a Dragon-level Wood elemental that required a sworn brotherhood of Dragon-Blooded to kill, and the Terrestrial crafter devoted a significant span of her life to creating while also using lots of other poisons and special firewood at great expense from across Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My read on that is that a more powerful Artifact <i>could</i> have been made, but the crafter opted for something more within their wheelhouse rather than let the concept and materials go to waste by risking failure on something more powerful.<br /> <br /> Similarly with the time, given how in the Artifact crafting rules, one isn't exactly bound to keeping at it after the mandatory first interval has been made; I would see the time and care as somewhere between a representation of needing to do other things to build up the craft points, and stunts to maximize the dice rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since the crafting rule doesn't require you to have materials from apocalyptic creature to make high rating Artifact</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The Artifact crafting rules don't lay out specifics for the necessary components, sure, but they do say that the Storyteller needs to adjudicate what the necessary tools and materials for any given project are, and that a project cannot begin until they are acquired.<br /> <br /> And I feel as though a Storyteller's surest guidelines on what the necessary materials are for any given Artifact are the stories describing other Artifacts.<br /> <br /> So I'd say that, while something like an ancient and powerful demon or the prison of an eldritch horror from before history or a powerful volcanic manse aren't necessarily the kinds of things that you need for a five-dot, it generally warrants something of approximately equivalent grandeur; I don't think that the Storyteller should allow somebody to run with a project for such a high level Artifact if all they have is a cave and a box of scraps. <br /> <br /> If nothing else, given how a consistent element of five-dot Artifact weapons appears to be &quot;this is an immense power that has its own ideas about how it should be used, and effectively using it can be a struggle even for the Exalted&quot;, I absolutely think that what it's made of (or the circumstances in which it was made) are at least as, if not more, important to the process as the skill of the maker, and that they should never be allowed just because the player has the gold points and the stats and they just want to pop out a thousand-year daiklave.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:19:58-07:00","id":1232402,"title":"","content":"The main reason that I want weak NPC to be possible Artifact ingredient (that doesn't sound creepy, right....?) is because some of them have pretty interesting theme that I would like to base my Evocation on, having to invent some super slime armor Behemoth for my 5-dot Artifact because Peronelle don't have enough magical oomph is not a problem if I have to do it once, but if I don't want to create a new uber NPC every time there is a non-powerful NPC with super awesome Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If nothing else, given how a consistent element of five-dot Artifact weapons appears to be &quot;this is an immense power that has its own ideas about how it should be used, and effectively using it can be a struggle even for the Exalted&quot;, I absolutely think that what it's made of (or the circumstances in which it was made) are at least as, if not more, important to the process as the skill of the maker, and that they should never be allowed just because the player has the gold points and the stats and they just want to pop out a thousand-year daiklave.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I just skimmed through the five-dot weapons and it's true that they all require the user to be careful when handling them, which is a shame since I prefer my Solar PCs to completely dominate their Artifact, the One Ring and Soul Edge gonna be my husbando whether they like it or not, all those corruption influences ain't gonna save them from my Zenith's pecs and Rose-Lipped Seduction Style. Since the Solar in my story are all elder, I guess I just gonna run them like that while other characters have to tip-toeing around Gorgon.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:13:47-07:00","id":1232420,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't really want you to look at things out of order, because I think that the way it's been going up until now has been good, so I'm going to put a pin in this topic and come back to it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T09:04:08-07:00","id":1234297,"title":"","content":"The next artifact is Heartsong, a Red Jade Powerbow.<br /> <br /> So Imban isn\u2019t a real word, but Chatelaine is, it\u2019s basically a <a href=\"https://3.bp.blogspot.com/-SFqlGOwvxfs/WohrA0oRppI/AAAAAAAAp_U/_gvJjuY9Gdcw3ySyCRnrz5EncUDO7sqPACLcBGAs/s1600/chatelaine%2Bcha1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">chain </a>with small tools used by a European ladies and them are soooo pretty, what even more interesting is that some ethnic groups in my country have a very similar accessory too, it\u2019s called <a href=\"http://langvietonline.vn/Uploads/Images/0/31b/031b864806eb04797fc8bd76b7856b9c.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">x\u00e0 t\u00edch</a>, aside from assisting in a lady chores they are also used to prepare tr\u1ea7u can (it\u2019s called paan win English according to wiki), just put the ingredient in the box and takes them out to chew whenever you are bored, or make a paan roll and give them to that handsome man over there (yeah, paan has a certain connotation of romance and marriage in my country for some strange reasons\u2026). And now I want to make an Artifact chain called A Lady\u2019s Best Friend which help you in Crafting, doing chores, being super cute and murdering your husband in his sleep since it\u2019s compatible with Dreaming Pearl Courtesan.<br /> <br /> So one of the ingredients for Heartsong is the two Fair Folk\u2019s love for each other, I kinda wonder how exactly do PC collect these things IC without Words-as-Workshop Method.<br /> <br /> Oh, so this is Eros\u2019s bow, isn\u2019t it? People who get hit by it are either filled with passion or with hatred, less nasty than Eros though without the \u201cFirst person you see after being hit is your affection target\u201d clause.<br /> <br /> And that illustration, I said not to comment on the art early, but this is such a waste of opportunity, we got a Greek-theme Artifact right here and the guy in the art is so not very good-looking, where are my <a href=\"http://The next artifact is Heartsong, a Red Jade Powerbow, the name reminds me of a Second Edition Artifact from the Infernal book, a harp that targets the victim heartsong I think, basically something about everybody having some kind of true song with them and the harp mess with it. Which makes me think whether Exalted follows the Buddhism or Hinduism concept of atman, which also makes me think about the lack of Buddhism things in Exalted (noooo, Shaolin monk ain\u2019t what Buddhism is about, neither is genocide death cult). Aaaanyway, so Imban isn\u2019t a real word, but Chatelaine is, it\u2019s basically a chain with small tools used by a European ladies and they are soooo pretty, what even more interesting is that some ethnic groups in my country has a very similar accessory too, it\u2019s called x\u00e0 t\u00edch, aside from assisting in a lady choresthey are also used to prepare tr\u1ea7u cau (it\u2019s called paan win English according to wiki), just put the ingredient in the box and takes them out to chew whenever you are bore, or make a paan roll and give them to that handsome man over there (yeah, paan has a certain connation of romance and marriage in my country for some strange reasons\u2026). And now I want to make an Artifact chain called A Lady\u2019s Best Friend which help you in Crafting, doing chores, being super cute and murdering your husband in his sleep since it\u2019s compatible with Dreaming Pearl Courtesan.So one of the ingredient for Heartsong is the two Fair Folk\u2019s love for each other, I kinda wonder how exactly do PC collect these things IC without Words-as-Workshop Method.Oh, so this is Eros\u2019s bow, isn\u2019t it? People who gets hit by it are either filled with passion or with hatred, less nasty than Eros though without the \u201cFirst person you see after being hit is your affection target\u201d clause.And that illustration, I said not to comment on the art early, but this is such a waste of opportunity, we got a Greek-theme Artifact right here and the guy in the art is so not very good-looking, where is my exposed pecs and abs????? I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing a Shen-version of Eros either, instead there is just some farmer dude on a cloud, this doesn\u2019t sell me on the weapon at all.Ha! An Eros bow that inflicts a Psyche effect on the target!Yike, Ardor-Sharing Technique is such a speedbump, 1m for 1 success, yay it\u2019s cheaper than an Excellen\u2026wait there is another requirement so it\u2019s easier to just use the Excellency, and the charm is also the preg for the whole tree\u2026\u2026\u2026I\u2019m starting to dislike this the weapon.The rest of the tree is how very so-so, it\u2019s not bad or anything, just super boring, none of the effect makes me go WOW I WANT TO USE THAT IN A FIGHT!!!?Conclusion: I\u2019m starting out super excited for this weapon but then get a massive disappointment (with great help from artwork farmer dude). To think that a Greek and Love-theme weapon contains absolutely no Jen\u2026\u2026 when this book is good, it\u2019s good, but when it\u2019s bad\u2026\u2026.you get Heartsong.\" target=\"_blank\">exposed pecs and abs</a>????? Does this book even has any hot dudes in it???!!<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing a Shen-version of Eros either, instead, there is just some farmer dude on a cloud, this doesn\u2019t sell me on the weapon at all.<br /> <br /> Ha! An Eros bow that inflicts a Psyche effect on the target!<br /> <br /> Yike, Ardor-Sharing Technique is such a speedbump, 1m for 1 success, yay it\u2019s cheaper than an Excellen\u2026wait there is another requirement so it\u2019s easier to just use the Excellency, and the charm is also the preg for the whole tree\u2026\u2026\u2026I\u2019m starting to dislike this weapon.<br /> <br /> The rest of the tree is how very so-so, it\u2019s not bad or anything, just super boring, none of the effects makes me go WOW I WANT TO USE THAT IN A FIGHT!!!?<br /> <br /> Conclusion: I\u2019m starting out super excited about this weapon but then get a massive disappointment (with great help from artwork farmer dude). To think that a Greek and Love-theme weapon contains absolutely no Jen\u2026\u2026 when this book is good, it\u2019s good, but when it\u2019s bad\u2026\u2026.you get...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QLh7D8z.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> ...Heartsong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T13:08:44-07:00","id":1234373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1234297#post1234297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So one of the ingredients for Heartsong is the two Fair Folk\u2019s love for each other, I kinda wonder how exactly do PC collect these things IC without Words-as-Workshop Method.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case it probably helps that they're being made from the actual bodies.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous workings probably help in a few cases, and maybe recruiting the assistance of supernatural creatures, but I think that for a lot of more basic things it can just be handwaved as doing some minor thing that justifies the Occult prerequisite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T15:02:31-07:00","id":1234416,"title":"","content":"Now now, Ardor-Sharing Technique is only bad if you don't want to screw with people's emotions mid-fight. If that's your thing, Heartsong is the bow for you!<br /> <br /> Your target is an Earth Aspect Immaculate Monk with Resolve 5 - pushing the very limits of human stoicism! The difficulty of a Passion-Inducing Gambit is Resolve-2. Ardor-Sharing Technique adds one automatic success, meaning you only need 2 successes to Inspire love in him - or force him to spend a willpower against it. You can't decide how he reacts to getting love fired into his heart, but once you get to Lover's Quarrel, you can! <br /> <br /> Plus, being Archery attacks, you can combo all this with Solar Archery, using Arrow Storm Technique to fire hatred (or smug indifference) into the hearts of six different opponents and then breaking off to let them deal with it.<br /> <br /> That probably doesn't improve its chances of being your bowfriend, (neither the weapon nor the wielder are beefy enough, I think), but it's not as bad as you'd think. Being able to just shoot emotional lleverage into your rivals is a neat trick, if you're playing that kinda guy.<br /> <br /> At the risk of explaining the joke, &quot;Lover's Quarrel&quot; is a pun that a non-native speaker might not get. A quarrel can mean both &quot;an argument&quot; (usually between people that are otherwise friendly) and &quot;a crossbow bolt&quot;, which fits nicely for an Eros-bow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","user":"Amayad","date":". 07-12-2018, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T21:58:11-07:00","id":1234537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1234416#post1234416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now now, Ardor-Sharing Technique is only bad if you don't want to screw with people's emotions mid-fight. If that's your thing, Heartsong is the bow for you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeaaah, but I'm one of those sad people who have never play in an Exalted before (and probably never will), so Charms whose effect is basically &quot;Pay 1 mote, get 1 sux&quot; are not very useful to me when drawing Exalted comic orz<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend?p=1234416#post1234416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of explaining the joke, &quot;Lover's Quarrel&quot; is a pun that a non-native speaker might not get. A quarrel can mean both &quot;an argument&quot; (usually between people that are otherwise friendly) and &quot;a crossbow bolt&quot;, which fits nicely for an Eros-bow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, aaah, I remembered a poster here saying that Charm is some kind of joke but the first definition that I found only contain the argument bit so I just sit there puzzled on what the joke is........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T23:31:44-07:00","id":1234547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\